nd $70%$ of biology students are female, what is the probability that a randomly selected student from class $3$ takes biology? Round your answer to $3$ decimal places.\n\n> A calculator is required to answer this question." :question/requires-calculator true}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186167118 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166877 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "6c467adb-9d0e-5b33-b81e-4959e2703535" :knowledge-point/title "Applying Bayes’ Theorem to a Situation in Context"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "88acdedb-86f7-5376-9663-ed92e647a982" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.174" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186163787} {:answer/id #uuid "b8298e93-12cb-5948-9b0c-4d75b7d3a684" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.199" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186163788} {:answer/id #uuid "cca46cae-3f7b-5c75-a82f-2a44e0f21afb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.203" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186163789} {:answer/id #uuid "1bae2866-554f-511e-86e4-7f2ca81b63aa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.13" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186163790} {:answer/id #uuid "7352704f-f734-5a12-b655-8b2ef85bf0d6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.191" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186163791}] :answer-field/id #uuid "42a0e7e2-d14d-5d36-a9fb-b4d391b04b02" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186163786}] :question/id #uuid "dea495bf-07d9-54cd-baea-bb953539d3dd" :question/math-academy-id "q-148673" :question/problem "Arthur and Sara are finding the best recipe for chocolate muffins, and they test three different oven cooking modes, mode $1$, mode $2$, and mode $3$. They also try two types of yeast, A and B.\n\n- They use mode $1$ to cook the $30%$ of their muffins, and $90%$ of those muffins turn out well.\n- They use mode $2$ to cook the $40%$ of their muffins, and $85%$ of those muffins turn out well.\n- They use mode $3$ to cook the $30%$ of their muffins, and $88%$ of those muffins turn out well.\n\nIf $20%$ of all muffins was prepared with yeast A, and $87%$ of yeast A muffins turn out well, what is the probability that a randomly chosen good muffin is done with yeast A? Round your answer to $3$ decimal places.\n\n> A calculator is required to answer this question." :question/requires-calculator true}]}
